      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Express $-\\frac{3}{4}\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{10}\\right)+\\frac{3}{4}\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{10}\\right)$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&-\\frac{3}{4}\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{10}\\right)+\\frac{3}{4}\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{10}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{3}{4}\\left(\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{10}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{10}\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x-\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{13\\pi}{10}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{10}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{10}\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{13\\pi}{10}\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{5}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3}{4}\\left(\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{10}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{10}\\right)\\right)&=\\frac{3}{4}\\cos\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{5}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
